## local.properties template for Android Studio / Gradle builds
##
## This file must NOT be committed with a hardcoded computer-specific path.
## Android Studio normally auto-creates local.properties when you open the project.
## If Android Studio shows "SDK location not found", create a 'local.properties'
## file in this project root directory and set sdk.dir to your local Android SDK path.
##
## Common SDK locations:
##
## Windows (replace <Username> with your Windows user name):
## sdk.dir=C\:\\Users\\<Username>\\AppData\\Local\\Android\\Sdk
##
## macOS:
## sdk.dir=/Users/<Username>/Library/Android/sdk
##
## Linux:
## sdk.dir=/home/<Username>/Android/Sdk
##
## Alternatively, set the ANDROID_HOME or ANDROID_SDK_ROOT environment variable on your computer.
